      "hints": [
        "Equate $2x^2 + 5 = mx - 3 \\implies 2x^2 - mx + 8 = 0$.",
        "Set discriminant $\\Delta = (-m)^2 - 4(2)(8) < 0$ and solve for $m$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Equate the curve and straight line equations to find points of intersection:\n$$2x^2 + 5 = mx - 3 \\implies 2x^2 - mx + 8 = 0$$",
        "Apply the condition for no real intersections (strictly negative discriminant $\\Delta < 0$):\n$$b^2 - 4ac < 0 \\implies (-m)^2 - 4(2)(8) < 0 \\implies m^2 - 64 < 0$$",
        "Solve the quadratic inequality for $m$:\n$$(m - 8)(m + 8) < 0 \\implies -8 < m < 8 \\quad (\\text{or } (-8, 8))$$"
      ],
